cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the preprint (link to be added when it is posted) and this repository."
title: "Why T5 keeps its OFF responses when its inputs are silenced in the FlyVis models: code and results of the later study"
abstract: "The later study (Section 5) of the preprint: in the 46 confirmation FlyVis models, silences T5's four OFF inputs (Tm1, Tm2, Tm4, Tm9) and cuts their routes onto T5 and CT1, under a corrected measurement (silencing held from rest, evoked response), to test whether T5's robustness to their silencing depends on the measurement and what accounts for it, under a protocol frozen before the run."
authors:
